{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880939-\u200bideas-for-a-silver-fang-macro-prelude","id":880939,"title":"\u200bIdeas for a Silver Fang Macro-Prelude.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-03T06:48:06-07:00","id":880939,"title":"\u200bIdeas for a Silver Fang Macro-Prelude.","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> I started a chronicle a couple of game session ago and I\u2019m adding a new PC. She\u2019s a Pure breed 5, female, recent mother 19 years old. She\u2019s niece of Lord Albrecht (Still not bane from Morningkill\u2019s caern).<br /> <br /> I need an extended prelude (or mini story) for her to catch up in XP with the other PCs.<br /> <br /> The main story for the pack all together is going to be either \u201cWar of the Amazon\u201d or the \u201cSkin Dancers\u201d, still to be decided.<br /> <br /> At the same time the pack plays its story I want to make them involved here and there with the Silver Crown story, mainly by the relationship between this PC and Albrecht. <br /> <br /> Any idea for the Prelude? I expect it to last for 4-6 hours of player-Story teller play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T18:25:37-07:00","id":881394,"title":"","content":"So one idea that I've been running with a solo Silver Fang involves issues from the family's past. The Silver Fang is personally haunted, he's convinced Luna has cursed him particularly during a full moon. Things always seem to go wrong on those nights, and too often he has frenzied during this time. He is afraid of the dark, and his closet in particular. More then once he's noticed the presance of a shadowy figure from the corner of his eye and felt his hair stand on end. He'd sleep out in the wild but he's nervous of being under Luna's light. Garou around him judge him rather harshly, as he looks like some of the worst stereotypes Fangs can produce. He is alone as clearly he's just that mad. So what's up?<br /> <br /> Has to do with an old family grudge. Back in the 1880's a Fang kin had both too low of a pure breed to be worth anything, and was a bit too &quot;touched&quot; so his kin family had him committed to an asylum where he was stuck with Victorian age therapies. He we left angry and feeling betrayed by his family (who were not exactly the image of mental health themselves). During his time in the institution he was noticed and embraced by a Malkavian (Lore of the Clans has some fun powers if you want to use a Malk as a villian to mess with people). This kin has gone on swearing to mentally break every prominent son from his family from then on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:04:44-07:00","id":881931,"title":"","content":"Thank you. This gave me a very good idea. The character has the flaw of &quot;Vengeance&quot; against a powerful vampire.<br /> I'm thinking of making the character going through a Rite of Passage in the Umbra where he learns about this Vampire and what he's doing to his family (in my story he will be trying to embrace werewolves and he believes this family has higher changes to survive the embrace) so she starts her quest against him.<br /> <br /> Where in the Umbra is the right place for the PC to learn about this? I Recall the Legendary realm only contain legends 2 centuries or older.<br /> I could, obviously, made up a realm only to host this story, but if something appropriate exists I would prefer to use the existing one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}